#
# /lib/ndb/local — the network database TEMPLATE (15-08, D-16).
#
# SUBSTITUTED at bake time by build/x86_64/mkimage.sh's payload section
# into the staged tree's /lib/ndb/local: the netaddr seam
# (root-tree/lib/netaddr.rc, the 14-09 D-11 single seam) is sourced and
# the tokens below are sedded from its slirp-leg keys —
#   @GUESTV4@  <- slirp_guestv4   the guest's own address
#   @MASKV4@   <- slirp_maskv4    the leg's mask
#   @GWV4@     <- slirp_gwv4      the leg's gateway
#   @ETHER@    <- ether           the NIC MAC (netaddr.rc's own
#                                 18-04 AUTH-05 key — the qemu-default
#                                 MAC's single home)
# The bake asserts the substituted file carries the seam's values and
# ZERO leftover tokens; this template itself carries NO venue address
# literal by construction (the bake's seam grep over root-tree/lib
# stays clean — a literal here fails the bake).
#
# Content model: the baked host entry is the same ip=/dom=/sys= tuple
# shape the 15-02 services probes measured cs answering from
# (`!ipinfo dom=host attr').  The mask and gateway ride as their own
# attribute tuples, and since 18-04 (AUTH-05) the Phase-18 extension
# point named in the old header has LANDED as the ipnet= row below:
# the auth composition (`!authdom=X auth=*' answers straight from the
# ndb — cs.c's generic pair parser; dns never intercepts non-dom/ip
# keys) + the host tuple's ether= attribute.  The auth row's tokens
# (prose names them WITHOUT the at-sign delimiters — the bake's
# zero-leftover-token assert greps the WHOLE file and comment prose
# counts too, the 15-07 lesson):
#   AUTHDOM  <- the authdomain-gen run's own authdom (the bake's
#               generator -i output — DEMO-harvey on the DEMO path,
#               never a seam value: the domain is PER-BAKE paired
#               material, and a seam key would be a second source
#               violating D-02's pairing)
#   auth=127.0.0.1  the loopback CONSTANT — template-legal (the only
#                 numeric literal in this file's AUTH-05 rows; not a
#                 venue address, the loopback probe's own address)
#
# 18-04's split: the AUTH bake (mkimage §14) substitutes ALL five
# tokens; the services bake (section P) substitutes the seam's four
# and STRIPS the auth row (its image has no domain — an authdom row
# without keys behind it would be a lie), asserting the strip BOTH
# ways (no authdom= in its output, zero leftover tokens).  Additive
# rows only — the services path's existing rows are byte-untouched.
#

ip=@GUESTV4@ sys=harvey dom=harvey.local ether=@ETHER@
ipmask=@MASKV4@
ipgw=@GWV4@
ipnet=harveynet ipmask=@MASKV4@ ipgw=@GWV4@ authdom=@AUTHDOM@ auth=127.0.0.1
